From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 19:02:33 -0300
Subject: drm/amdgpu: expand DC stream timing for frame-packing stereo modes

A DRM frame-packing mode is expressed per-eye (1920x1080@24), but its
framebuffer carries both views: 1080 left-eye lines, the 45-line vertical
gap, then 1080 right-eye lines, 2205 lines in total. amdgpu's legacy
SetCrtc path sizes the primary plane via drm_mode_get_hv_timing(), while
the DC stream is created from the unadjusted per-eye mode and DC's CRTC
mode_fixup() is a no-op, so DC scanned a 1080-line 74.25 MHz timing against
a 2205-line plane: the sink entered 3D on a valid FP VSIF and showed black
(recorded on the same hardware as patch 1).

When the mode carries DRM_MODE_FLAG_3D_FRAME_PACKING, apply
drm_mode_set_crtcinfo(..., CRTC_STEREO_DOUBLE) to the stream mode and size
the stream rectangle with drm_mode_get_hv_timing(), as nouveau has done
since its 2017 HDMI stereoscopy series and i915 does today. DC then
receives 1920/2750 horizontal and 2205/2250 vertical at 148.5 MHz for
1080p24 FP, and the packed surface scans out as intended. DC's dormant
stereo view formats stay disabled: this is one userspace-packed surface,
with the FP VSIF from patch 1 identifying it to the sink.

Ported to 7.3 (amdgpu_dm_connector.c); the change itself is unchanged.

Link: https://github.com/danielcamposramos/sony-bravia-linux (tools, run logs and evidence)
Assisted-by: LLM Kimi K3 (Codex CLI)
Assisted-by: LLM GPT 5.6 Sol (Codex CLI)
Assisted-by: LLM Claude Opus 5 (Claude Code CLI)
(cherry picked from commit 8ebc9d5e768e1b0df96f25a74653a340a923ad3e)
---
 .../amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c  | 16 +++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
index 587813dc04198e46b1ed8d0f2116151bad26d1d1..0f819418f4dc62de9111c23b18f166a3957e9b21 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
@@ -1420,9 +1420,8 @@ void amdgpu_dm_update_stream_scaling_settings(struct drm_device *dev,
 	if (!mode)
 		return;
 
-	/* Full screen scaling by default */
-	src.width = mode->hdisplay;
-	src.height = mode->vdisplay;
+	/* Include the second eye in frame-packing scanout geometry. */
+	drm_mode_get_hv_timing(mode, &src.width, &src.height);
 	dst.width = stream->timing.h_addressable;
 	dst.height = stream->timing.v_addressable;
 
@@ -1571,6 +1570,17 @@ create_stream_for_sink(struct drm_connector *connector,
 		}
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * DRM frame-packing modes describe one eye. Userspace presents both
+	 * eyes in one buffer, so DC must see the expanded link timing too.
+	 */
+	if (mode.flags & DRM_MODE_FLAG_3D_FRAME_PACKING) {
+		drm_mode_set_crtcinfo(&mode, CRTC_STEREO_DOUBLE);
+		drm_dbg_kms(dev, "expanded HDMI frame-packing timing to %dx%d total %dx%d clock %d kHz\n",
+			    mode.crtc_hdisplay, mode.crtc_vdisplay,
+			    mode.crtc_htotal, mode.crtc_vtotal, mode.crtc_clock);
+	}
+
 	if (recalculate_timing)
 		drm_mode_set_crtcinfo(&saved_mode, 0);
 
